@base = http://localhost:8080

# Run reset.sql first, then the requests in order: ids and results depend on it.
# Accounts (reset.sql): mina and omar are USER, admin is ADMIN. Passwords: name + 1234.
#   Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==  is mina:mina1234
#   Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==  is omar:omar1234
#   Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0  is admin:admin1234
# Reading rooms is public. Only admin creates, changes or deletes rooms. Booking needs a login,
# and the owner is the caller. Every error answer has the ApiError body:
# {"timestamp": "...", "status": 404, "error": "Not Found", "message": "...", "path": "..."}

########## GET /api/rooms — list, with optional filters ##########

### 1. List all rooms (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms

### 2. Filter by minimum capacity (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms?minCapacity=15

### 3. Filter by keyword in the name (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms?keyword=room

### 4. Both filters together (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms?minCapacity=15&keyword=room

### 5. Filters that match nothing — empty list (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms?minCapacity=15&keyword=nothing

### 6. minCapacity is not a number (400)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms?minCapacity=abc

########## GET /api/rooms/{id} — one room ##########

### 7. Get one room (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/1

########## POST /api/rooms — create (admin) ##########

### 8. Create a room as admin (201 + Location: /api/rooms/4)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Room C", "capacity": 8}

########## PUT /api/rooms/{id} — update (admin) ##########

### 9. Update the new room (200; one select, one update)
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/4
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Room C (renamed)", "capacity": 12}

### 10. Update a room that does not exist (404)
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/999
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Nope", "capacity": 10}

########## DELETE /api/rooms/{id} (admin) ##########

### 11. Delete the new room (204)
DELETE {{base}}/api/rooms/4
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0

### 12. Delete a room that does not exist (404)
DELETE {{base}}/api/rooms/999
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0

########## Validation and statistics ##########

### 13. Create with capacity 50 (400)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Too big", "capacity": 50}

### 14. Count rooms (200, {"rooms": 3})
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/stats

########## Week 7 — reservations ##########

### 15. Reservations for room 1 (200, 3 items, each with its owner)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations

### 16. Reservations for a missing room (404)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/99/reservations

### 17. mina books room 1, 14 Oct 10–11 (201 + Location: /api/reservations/6, owner mina)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-10-14T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-14T11:00:00"}

### 18. Overlaps reservation 1, 6 Oct 10:30–11:30 (409)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-10-06T10:30:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T11:30:00"}

### 19. Starts when reservation 1 ends, 6 Oct 11:00–12:00 (201 + Location: /api/reservations/7)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-10-06T11:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T12:00:00"}

### 20. End before start (400)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-10-06T12:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T11:00:00"}

### 21. Book a missing room (404)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/99/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-10-06T12:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T13:00:00"}

### 22. mina's reservations (200, 4 items: ids 3, 1, 7, 6; one select)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/mine
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

### 23. Delete a room with reservations (409)
DELETE {{base}}/api/rooms/1
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0

########## Assignment 5 — one reservation ##########

### 24. Get mina's reservation 6 (200; the Location from 17 now opens)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/6
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

### 25. mina cancels her reservation 7 (204)
DELETE {{base}}/api/reservations/7
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

########## Week 9 — dirty checking and ApiError ##########

### 26. Update room 2 with the same values (200; one select, no update)
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/2
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Study Pod", "capacity": 4}

### 27. Update room 2 to Study Pod XL, 6 (200; select + update, no save())
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/2
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Study Pod XL", "capacity": 6}

### 28. Create a room with a blank name (400, name is required)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "  ", "capacity": 5}

### 29. Create a room with capacity 0 (400, capacity must be between 1 and 20)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Closet", "capacity": 0}

### 30. Blank name and capacity 50 (400, name is required: checked first)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "", "capacity": 50}

### 31. Get a room that does not exist (404, Room 99 not found)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/99

### 32. Delete room 1, which has reservations (409, Room 1 has reservations)
DELETE {{base}}/api/rooms/1
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0

### 33. A URL with no endpoint (404, not 500)
GET {{base}}/api/nothing

### 34. mina books room 2 and sends a reservedBy (201 + Location: /api/reservations/8; owner mina, reservedBy is ignored)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/2/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"reservedBy": "omar", "startTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-20T11:00:00"}

### 35. Book without endTime (400, startTime and endTime are required)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/2/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-10-21T10:00:00"}

### 36. End before start (400, startTime must be before endTime)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/2/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-10-21T12:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-21T11:00:00"}

### 37. Over reservation 1, 6 Oct 10:00–11:00 (409, already reserved)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-10-06T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T11:00:00"}

### 38. Get a reservation that does not exist (404, Reservation 99 not found)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/99
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

### 39. Reservation id is not a number (400, 'id' has an invalid value)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/abc
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

### 40. Create a room with capacity "ten" (400, not valid JSON)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Lab", "capacity": "ten"}

### 41. Room id is not a number (400, 'id' has an invalid value)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/abc

########## Week 10 — HTTP Basic and sign-up ##########

### 42. Create a room without logging in (401, login required)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "No login", "capacity": 4}

### 43. Sign up lee (201; id, username and role USER, no password and no hash)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "lee", "password": "lee12345"}

### 44. Sign up lee again (409, username lee is taken)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "lee", "password": "lee12345"}

### 45. Bad username and a short password (400, both problems in the message)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "Lee!", "password": "short"}

### 46. Create a room as lee with Basic (403, admin role required: lee is USER)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic bGVlOmxlZTEyMzQ1
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Lee's Room", "capacity": 6}

### 47. Create a room with a wrong password (401, wrong username or password)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic bGVlOndyb25ncGFzcw==
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Wrong password", "capacity": 6}

### 48. List rooms without logging in (200, 3 rooms)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms

### 49. Who am I, with Basic (200, lee, ROLE_USER)
GET {{base}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic bGVlOmxlZTEyMzQ1

########## Week 10 — tokens ##########

### 50. Log in as lee (200, accessToken; kept as {{token}})
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "lee", "password": "lee12345"}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken); %}

### 51. Log in with a wrong password (401, wrong username or password)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "lee", "password": "wrongpass"}

### 52. Who am I, with the token (200, lee, ROLE_USER from the role claim)
GET {{base}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 53. Create a room with lee's token (403, admin role required)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Token Room", "capacity": 5}

### 54. Create a room with a broken token (401, token is invalid or expired)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.broken.token
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Broken token", "capacity": 5}

### 55. List rooms with a broken token (401: a token that is sent is always checked)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.broken.token

### 56. Reservations without logging in (401, login required)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/mine

########## Week 11 — roles (rule D) ##########

### 57. Sign up and ask to be ADMIN (201, role USER: the role field is ignored)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "eve", "password": "eve12345", "role": "ADMIN"}

### 58. Log in as admin (200; kept as {{adminToken}})
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "admin", "password": "admin1234"}

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 59. Who am I, with the admin token (200, admin, ROLE_ADMIN)
GET {{base}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 60. Create a room with the admin token (201 + Location: /api/rooms/5)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Admin Room", "capacity": 10}

### 61. Create a room as mina (403, admin role required)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Mina's Room", "capacity": 4}

### 62. Update room 5 with lee's token (403, admin role required)
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Lee's now", "capacity": 4}

### 63. Delete room 5 without logging in (401, login required)
DELETE {{base}}/api/rooms/5

########## Week 11 — owners (rule C) ##########

### 64. mina books room 5 (201 + Location: /api/reservations/9, owner mina)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/5/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-11-23T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-23T11:00:00"}

### 65. Delete room 5 with the admin token (409, Room 5 has reservations)
DELETE {{base}}/api/rooms/5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 66. mina's reservations (200, 5 items: ids 3, 1, 6, 8, 9)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/mine
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

### 67. omar's reservations (200, 3 items: ids 2, 4, 5)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/mine
Authorization: Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==

### 68. omar reads mina's reservation 9 (403, reservation 9 belongs to another user)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==

### 69. admin reads reservation 9 (200)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 70. omar cancels mina's reservation 9 (403)
DELETE {{base}}/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==

### 71. omar reads a reservation that does not exist (404)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/99
Authorization: Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==

########## Lab G — PUT /api/reservations/{id}, owner only ##########

### 72. mina moves 9 to 14:00–15:00 (200)
PUT {{base}}/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-11-23T14:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-23T15:00:00"}

### 73. mina moves 9 to the same time (200: a reservation never overlaps itself)
PUT {{base}}/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-11-23T14:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-23T15:00:00"}

### 74. omar moves mina's 9 (403, reservation 9 belongs to another user)
PUT {{base}}/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-11-23T16:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-23T17:00:00"}

### 75. admin moves mina's 9 (403: owner only, not even an admin)
PUT {{base}}/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-11-23T16:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-23T17:00:00"}

### 76. mina moves 6 onto 10:30 on 6 Oct (409, Room 1 is already reserved at that time)
PUT {{base}}/api/reservations/6
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-10-06T10:30:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T11:30:00"}

### 77. mina moves 9 with end before start (400)
PUT {{base}}/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-11-23T15:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-23T14:00:00"}

### 78. mina moves a reservation that does not exist (404)
PUT {{base}}/api/reservations/99
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-11-23T14:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-23T15:00:00"}

### 79. admin cancels reservation 9 (204)
DELETE {{base}}/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 80. admin deletes room 5, now empty (204)
DELETE {{base}}/api/rooms/5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

########## Week 11 — CORS ##########

### 81. Preflight from http://localhost:5500 (200 + Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:5500)
OPTIONS {{base}}/api/rooms
Origin: http://localhost:5500
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Authorization, Content-Type

### 82. Preflight from another site (403, plain text "Invalid CORS request")
OPTIONS {{base}}/api/rooms
Origin: http://evil.example.com
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Authorization, Content-Type

########## My own failure requests ##########

### 83. Zero-length booking: start equals end (400)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/3/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00"}

### 84. Bad capacity on a missing room (400, not 404: the body is checked before the room is loaded)
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/99
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Nope", "capacity": 0}

########## Optional challenge — refresh token ##########

### 85. Exchange the refresh token from 50 for new tokens (200; the old refresh token is deleted)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"}

> {% client.global.set("oldRefreshToken", client.global.get("refreshToken")); client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken); %}

### 86. The old refresh token again (401, token is invalid or expired: it was used once)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{oldRefreshToken}}"}

### 87. Log out: delete the refresh token (204)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"}

### 88. Refresh after logout (401, token is invalid or expired)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"}
